      235: 	<section id="open">
      236: 		<h2>Open questions</h2>
      237: 		<ul>
      238: 			<li><strong>Budget unit.</strong> Is the 200k a prompt ceiling you want enforced with a token estimate, or is the diff budget a separate smaller number? A token estimate is fuzzy without a tokenizer; bytes are exact and hermetic.</li>
      239: 			<li><strong>Where the cap lives.</strong> Option A is a pure function in the core and needs no boundary change. Option B is the right boundary but adds <code>diffStat</code> and a <code>filesets</code> option on <code>Jj.diff</code>. Which do you want first?</li>
      240: 			<li><strong>Granularity.</strong> Per-file, or per-hunk? Keeping the first hunk of every large file preserves a hint of what changed; it also makes the output shape less predictable.</li>
      241: 			<li><strong>Default ignore list.</strong> Do lockfiles and generated output get a shipped default, or does the user opt in? A shipped default changes existing stamps.</li>
      242: 			<li><strong>Fallback shape.</strong> When even the condensed diff overflows, should the header generator run with paths only, or should the stamp skip the subagent and use <code>deriveSubject</code> up front instead of after three failed calls?</li>
      243: 		</ul>
