      198: /**
      199:  * Collect a diff under `budget`, emitting one `diff-condensed` status when
      200:  * content was dropped.
      201:  *
      202:  * A path matching `budget.omit` keeps its name and change count and loses its
      203:  * content whatever its size. Otherwise a file over `maxLinesPerFile` loses its
      204:  * content, and content is fetched in file order until the estimated-token
      205:  * budget is spent, after which every remaining file is name-only.
      206:  *
      207:  * The caller keeps its own failure policy: a read that rejects propagates, so
      208:  * a diff-only stamp can report `diff_fetch_failed` while an interaction stamp
      209:  * can degrade to an empty diff.
      210:  */
      211: export async function collectDiff(
      212: 	jj: Jj,
      213: 	spec: DiffSpec,
      214: 	budget: DiffBudget,
      215: 	cwd: string,
      216: 	onStatus?: (event: StatusEvent) => void,
      217: ): Promise<CollectedDiff> {
      218: 	const files = await jj.diffFiles(spec, { cwd });
